# BASS STEPS (0.16.29, GitHub issue #6): the LFO button's fifth page, after Bass line. Opened with none set, it holds the bar the line played last;
# a white key picks a step, the knobs set its kind (rest, note, accent, glide, accent + glide), its note (scale steps above the chord's root) and its
# octave, and an edit turns the bass line's mode (P_BL_MODE, 152) to Steps (16). Saved with the piece; another piece has its own (none: a rest).
seed 0
seamless 1
wait 3000
expect playing 1
tap LFO
tap LFO
tap LFO
tap LFO
wait 100
expect view 9
# the line in eighths for a couple of bars, so there is a bar to capture
spin K1 -20
spin K1 3
wait 4000
expect par152 3
tap LFO
wait 300
expect view 10
expect bsany 1
expect bskind0 1
expect bskind1 0
expect bskind2 1
shot basssteps.png
# step 3 (the third white key, key 4): an accent on the fifth (four scale steps up), an octave up
tapkey 4
spin K1 -10
spin K1 2
wait 100
expect bskind2 2
spin K2 -10
spin K2 4
wait 100
expect bsnote2 4
spin K3 -5
spin K3 2
wait 100
expect bsoct2 2
expect par152 16
wait 2000
expect bspos >-1
# step 5: a glide
tapkey 7
spin K1 -10
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect bskind4 3
# saved with the piece, back after a power-on
tap GLO
tap SAVE
wait 500
expect saved 1
tap PLAY
wait 5000
reboot
wait 3000
expect piece 0
expect par152 16
expect bskind2 2
expect bsnote2 4
expect bsoct2 2
expect bskind4 3
# another piece: its own (none set)
turn PRESET 1
wait 1500
expect piece 1
expect bsany 0
turn PRESET -1
wait 1500
expect bskind2 2
